  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site. Its workflow ends with step 7. That step sends the reader on to reassess stale records \"following the habeas-evidence skill\", and to its \"Disagreeing assessments\" section if assessments disagree. It then sends behavior or text changes to \"the habeas-requirements skill\". Both skills are bundled: `assets/skills/habeas-evidence` and `assets/skills/habeas-requirements` exist. Step 7 therefore names a skill for each follow-on task. The \"Gotchas\" section after the workflow only adds caveats and no new workflow step. The requirement is met.",
